[Event "Knight School"]
[Opening "London System"]
[Variation "Accelerated London System, mirror"]
[ECO "D00"]
[Character "solid,positional"]
[Risk "low"]
[EarlyMate "none"]
[Tricks "none"]
[Themes "break-symmetry,c4-break"]
[For "white"]
[Kind "sideline"]
[Opponent "2...Bf5"]
[Start "london-bf4-first 2.Bf4"]

2... Bf5 3. e3 e6 4. c4 { Both sides have the same bishops, so White breaks the symmetry: the c-pawn challenges d5 and pulls Black's centre apart. } 4... Nf6 ( 4... dxc4 5. Bxc4 ) ( 4... Bb4+ 5. Nd2 ) ( 4... c6 5. Qb3 ) ( 4... Bxb1 5. Qa4+ ) 5. Nf3 Bd6 6. Bxd6 { Trade the bishop here: the pawn recapture ...cxd6 gives Black a worse pawn structure, while White keeps a free hand. } 6... cxd6 7. cxd5 { Opens the c-file and leaves Black with a tricky isolated d-pawn to look after. } 7... Nxd5 8. Nbd2 *
